        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rings and Ideals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+====================================================================+\n|              THE RING HIERARCHY                                    |\n+====================================================================+\n|                                                                    |\n|  RING (R, +, ·): abelian group under +, monoid under ·, distrib.  |\n|    ↓ commutativity of ·                                            |\n|  COMMUTATIVE RING                                                  |\n|    ↓ no zero divisors (ab=0 → a=0 or b=0)                         |\n|  INTEGRAL DOMAIN                                                   |\n|    ↓ every nonzero element = unit (invertible)                     |\n|  FIELD (Q, R, C, F_p)                                             |\n|                                                                    |\n|  OR instead:                                                       |\n|  INTEGRAL DOMAIN                                                   |\n|    ↓ unique factorization into irreducibles                        |\n|  UFD (unique factorization domain)                                 |\n|    ↓ every ideal is principal (generated by one element)           |\n|  PID (principal ideal domain)                                      |\n|    ↓ Euclidean algorithm exists                                    |\n|  EUCLIDEAN DOMAIN                                                  |\n|    ↓ every nonzero element is a unit                               |\n|  FIELD                                                             |\n|                                                                    |\n|  Examples: Field → ED → PID → UFD → domain → ring                 |\n|  Z: ED (PID, UFD) but NOT a field.                                |\n|  Z[x]: UFD but NOT a PID (ideal (2,x) is not principal).          |\n|  Z[√-5]: domain, NOT UFD (6 = 2·3 = (1+√-5)(1-√-5)).             |\n+====================================================================+\n```"
    },
