        "root_concepts": "[rings, ideals]",
        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rings and Ideals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nA RING (R, +, ·) satisfies:\n  (R, +): abelian group (with identity 0)\n  (R, ·): monoid (with identity 1; associative; often commutative)\n  Distributivity: a(b+c) = ab+ac  and  (a+b)c = ac+bc."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md#006",
      "path": [
        "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals, git-history:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals]",
        "canonical_path": "abstract-algebra/04-RINGS-IDEALS.md",
        "concepts": "[rings, ideals]",
        "current_path": "abstract-algebra/04-RINGS-IDEALS.md",
        "id": "maxim:abstract-algebra:rings-ideals",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "abstract-algebra",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rings, ideals]",
        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rings and Ideals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Standard consequences:\n  0·a = 0 for all a (mdloom: 0·a = (0+0)·a = 0·a + 0·a → 0·a = 0)\n  (-1)·a = -a (mdloom: a + (-1)a = (1+(-1))a = 0·a = 0)\n  (-a)b = -(ab) = a(-b)"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md#007",
      "path": [
        "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals, git-history:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals]",
        "canonical_path": "abstract-algebra/04-RINGS-IDEALS.md",
        "concepts": "[rings, ideals]",
        "current_path": "abstract-algebra/04-RINGS-IDEALS.md",
        "id": "maxim:abstract-algebra:rings-ideals",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "abstract-algebra",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rings, ideals]",
        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rings and Ideals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "NOTE on \"1\": Some authors don't require a multiplicative identity.\n  A ring without 1 is a \"rng\" (ring without identity).\n  We always include 1 here."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals, git-history:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals]",
        "canonical_path": "abstract-algebra/04-RINGS-IDEALS.md",
        "concepts": "[rings, ideals]",
        "current_path": "abstract-algebra/04-RINGS-IDEALS.md",
        "id": "maxim:abstract-algebra:rings-ideals",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "abstract-algebra",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rings, ideals]",
        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rings and Ideals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Commutative ring: ab = ba for all a,b.\n  Almost all rings in algebraic number theory are commutative.\n  Matrix rings are the main non-commutative example.\n```"
    },
