        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rings and Ideals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCOMMUTATIVE RINGS:\n  Z — the prototype ring (integers).\n  Z/nZ — integers mod n.\n  Q, R, C — fields (every nonzero element invertible).\n  F_p = Z/pZ — finite field.\n  Z[x] — polynomials over integers.\n  Q[x], R[x], C[x] — polynomial rings over fields.\n  Z[i] = {a+bi : a,b ∈ Z} — Gaussian integers.\n  Z[√-5] — does not have unique factorization.\n  Z[ζ_n] — cyclotomic integers."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md#012",
      "path": [
        "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals, git-history:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals]",
        "canonical_path": "abstract-algebra/04-RINGS-IDEALS.md",
        "concepts": "[rings, ideals]",
        "current_path": "abstract-algebra/04-RINGS-IDEALS.md",
        "id": "maxim:abstract-algebra:rings-ideals",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "abstract-algebra",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rings, ideals]",
        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rings and Ideals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "NON-COMMUTATIVE RINGS:\n  M_n(F) — n×n matrices over field F.\n  H = {a+bi+cj+dk : a,b,c,d ∈ R} — quaternions.\n  Group ring R[G] = {Σ rₐ·a : rₐ ∈ R, a ∈ G, finite sum} with convolution multiplication.\n  Endomorphism ring End_R(M) of an R-module M."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md#013",
      "path": [
        "04-RINGS-IDEALS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals, git-history:abstract-algebra:04-rings-ideals]",
        "canonical_path": "abstract-algebra/04-RINGS-IDEALS.md",
