        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rings and Ideals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ZERO DIVISORS:\n  a ≠ 0 is a zero divisor if ∃b ≠ 0: ab = 0.\n  Z/6Z: 2·3 = 6 ≡ 0. Both 2 and 3 are zero divisors.\n  Z/pZ: no zero divisors (field).\n  M_n(F): if n≥2, zero divisors exist (e.g., rank-deficient matrices).\n```"
    },
