      "text": "EXAMPLES:\n  In Z: ideals are exactly nZ = (n) for n ≥ 0. Z is a PID.\n  In Z[x]: ideals (2) and (x) are principal; (2,x) is NOT principal.\n  In a field F: only ideals are (0) and F=(1). Consistent with: fields have no\n    nontrivial ideals (which is equivalent to being a field for commutative rings).\n```"
